# Node Express API Standards

- One router per resource; mount under versioned prefix (`/api/v1`)
- Async route handlers wrapped to forward errors to centralized middleware
{{#if parameters.typescript}}
- Use TypeScript with strict mode; typed request/response where practical
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.zodValidation}}
- Validate `body`, `query`, and `params` with Zod schemas at route entry
{{/if}}
- Never block the event loop with sync I/O in request path
- Return consistent error shape: `{ error: { code, message, details? } }`
{{#if parameters.structuredLogging}}
- Log as JSON with level, requestId, and duration; no secrets in logs
{{/if}}
- Use dependency injection or factory pattern for testable services
